<section class="pub-card" id="desktop"><h2>Use all three on your desktop</h2><p>Your desktop apps can keep the accounts signed in together. Microsoft account identities and storage remain distinct.</p><ol><li><strong>Outlook:</strong> Settings → Accounts → Your accounts → Add account. Add each address. In classic Outlook, use File → Add Account. Add Gmail through Google sign-in.</li><li><strong>Teams:</strong> select your profile → Add another account. All three can be available in the same app, subject to account access.</li><li><strong>OneDrive:</strong> Settings → Account → Add an account. One personal account and multiple eligible work or school accounts can be used together.</li></ol><p>Website authorization does not configure your Windows desktop or merge your accounts. Keep your existing Windows sign-in; separate Windows profiles are not required just to add mail accounts.</p></section>
